                <pb facs="0516" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg442"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 3.</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Extracts from the
                            boundary treaty between Costa Rica and Nicaragua</hi>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1858-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 15, 1858</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">“Article</hi> 2. The dividing line between the two
                    republics, beginning at the Sea of the North, (Caribbean,) shall commence in the
                    extremity of Castillo Point in the mouth of San Juan river, and shall run up
                    with the right bank of said river till to a point three English miles from
                    Castillo Viejo. * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">“Art.</hi> 4. The bay of San del Norte, like that of
                    Salinas, shall be common property of both republics.</p>
                <pb facs="0517" n="443" xml:id="pg443"/>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#small-caps">Art.</hi> 6. The republic of Nicaragua shall have
                    exclusive dominion and <hi rendition="#italic">summum imperium</hi> over the
                    waters of San Juan river from its issue out of the lake till to its mouth into
                    the Atlantic; but the republic of Costa Rica shall possess in said waters
                    forever the right of free navigation from said mouth up to within three miles of
                    Castillo Viejo.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
